# Ruin-Lurker Bat: the scry needs "you descended this turn" (CR 700.11). Turn 1 Bot1 casts the Bat (Mox Pearl) and nothing goes to its graveyard: at its end
# step the trigger is never put on the stack (the refusal: nothing to arrange). Turn 3 Faithless Looting discards an Ornithopter and a Plains from Bot1's
# hand, so it did descend that turn and the Bat scries one card (the positive control for the refusal): the Mountain goes to the bottom, so the draw on
# turn 5 is the Forest under it.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Pearl
Mox Ruby
Ruin-Lurker Bat
Faithless Looting
Mountain
Plains
Ornithopter
Plains
Island
Swamp
Mountain
Forest
Forest x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Ruin-Lurker Bat.Cast
[T1 Bot1.End]
Bot1.Pass
! Bot1.Arrange
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Faithless Looting.Cast
Bot1.Choose(Ornithopter; Plains)
[T3 Bot1.End]
Bot1.Arrange( | Mountain)
[T5 Bot1.Main1]

[Expect]
Bot1.Graveyard = Faithless Looting; Plains; Ornithopter
Bot1.Hand = Forest; Island; Mox Ruby; Plains; Swamp
